{% macro before(message, slots, ctx) -%}
{% if "directive_before" in slots and ctx.directive %}{{ directive(ctx.directive) }}{{ "\n\n---\n\n" }}{% endif -%}
{% if "context" in slots and ctx.title %}## Current Task
{{ ctx.task_ref }}{% if ctx.description %}{{ "\n" }}{{ ctx.description }}{% endif %}{{ "\n\n" }}{% endif -%}
{% if "input" in slots %}## Current Message
{% elif "opening" in slots %}## Opening Message
{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro after(message, slots, ctx) -%}
{% if "input" in slots %}{{ "\n\n" }}（Reply in the same language as the Current Message above.）{% endif -%}
{% if "directive_after" in slots and ctx.directive %}{{ "\n\n" }}{{ directive(ctx.directive) }}{% endif -%}
{% if "resources" in slots and ctx.capability_sections %}{{ "\n\n" }}{{ capabilities(ctx.capability_sections) }}{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro fresh(ctx) -%}
{% if ctx.title %}## Current Task
{{ ctx.task_ref }}{% if ctx.description %}{{ "\n" }}{{ ctx.description }}{% endif %}{% endif -%}
{% if ctx.user_prompt %}{% if ctx.title %}{{ "\n\n" }}{% endif %}## Current Message
{{ ctx.user_prompt }}

（Reply in the same language as the Current Message above.）{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro history_before(item) -%}
{% if item.summary_kind == "user" %}[The following is a compressed summary of earlier conversation and experience, given so you can carry the work forward; it is not a new instruction from the user.]
{% elif item.summary_kind == "assistant_current" %}{{ progress_heading }}
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro history_after(item) -%}
{% if item.summary_kind in ["assistant", "assistant_current"] %}

[The above is a system-written compressed summary of your earlier work, kept to carry context forward; it is not your reply to the user. Continue the current task from it and call tools as needed — do not imitate the summary's form when you answer.]{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro context_block(source) -%}
## {% if source.kind == "blackboard" %}Shared Context{% elif source.kind == "summary" %}Relevant Memory{% else %}Reference{% endif %}{% if source.metadata.get("title") %}: {{ source.metadata.title }}{% endif %}

{{ source.content }}{% if source.kind == "reference" and source.metadata.get("citation") %}

Source: {{ source.metadata.citation }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro role(body) -%}
{% if body %}## Your Current Role

{{ body }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro capability_pointer() -%}
(Your available capabilities — tools / skills / sub-agents — are listed in the Capabilities section of the current task message above.)
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro task_anchor(label) -%}
{% if label %}Current task: {{ label }}{% else %}Current task: (as framed in the conversation above){% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro subtasks(items) -%}
{% for task in items %}- {{ task.ref }} [{{ task.outcome }}]{% if task.note %} — {{ task.note }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro compact_fallback() -%}
You condense completed execution into a durable record that later turns or other agents can continue from. The trailing instruction defines this turn's scope, output shape, and submission channel; take those mechanics from there and the compression standard from here.

Write only from evidence visible in the conversation: tool calls and their results, files and data produced, and errors as returned. Distinguish attempted from achieved; do not treat the actor's narration of its own work as evidence. Never re-execute the work and never decide on the actor's behalf. Your record replaces the material it covers, so preserve what later work needs: user constraints; decisions already made and their reasons; unfinished threads and failure causes; the current goal; references to bulky evidence; and concrete state and findings sufficient to act on. Prefer these over step-by-step narrative. Carry forward what an earlier digest preserved instead of presenting it as new progress.
{%- endmacro %}
